Defining DB entities
DB design, like the whole application design, is organized in iterations. Let's suppose that,
in the first iteration, we need a prototype with two database tables: one for all the travel
packages and another one for all the locations referenced by the packages. Each package
covers just one location, while a single location may be covered by several packages, so the
two tables are connected by a one-to-many relationship.
