Therefore, it's good practice to add both of them to all the entity definitions.
Specifying which fields are obligatory and which ones are optional: By default,
all the reference types (such as all the strings) are assumed to be optional, while
all the value types (numbers and GUIDs, for instance) are assumed to be
obligatory. If we want a reference type to be obligatory, then we must decorate it
with the Required attribute. However, if we want a T value type property to be
optional, then we must replace it with T?.
